      "writtenOn": "2023-10-31T11:37:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "here supported means: \"anything we implement\", but a bit further below it means: \"implemented but without security issues\". Then there is preferred, which is a subset of \"implemented but without security issues\".\n\n\nCould we pick a definition, document it once and be consistent with it? eg.\n```\n// Algorithms blah blah. Algorithms can be \u0027supported\u0027 (implemented, without security issues), \u0027preferred\u0027 (a subset of supported, which we set as the default choice) and \u0027insecure\u0027 (implemented, but known weaknesses. Must be enabled explicitly)\ntype Algorithms struct {\n...\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "dff90d6fa676f462a243869f208601633b5262d4",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
